From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:55:38 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] model: keep shifted copies of formulas to 16 bytes

Most formula cells of a large sheet hold a shifted copy of a shared tree:
the tree's pointer and an offset. `Formula` still had room for an own
text, tree and legacy array range, 56 bytes, so each such cell cost a
72-byte allocation.

A formula of its own now keeps those in a box; a shifted copy is the
pointer and the offset, so `Formula` is 16 bytes and a shifted copy's
allocation 32. The legacy array range becomes `array()` /
`set_array()` / `with_array()`: a shifted copy is never an array formula,
and one made an array formula gets a text and tree of its own.
